.TH FACTOR 1
.SH NAME
factor \- factor a number, in Limbo
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B factor
[
.I number
\&...
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Factor
is a line-for-line Limbo translation of Plan 9's own
.IR factor (1)
.RB ( sys/src/cmd/factor.c ),
not a behavioral workalike reverse-engineered from a host tool - see
.B doc/plan9-port.md
in the source tree for the distinction, and
.IR primes (1),
a companion port from the same source file family. It lives under
.B p9/cmd
rather than
.BR appl/cmd ;
see
.B p9/dis/README
for how to bind it in.
.PP
With arguments,
.I factor
prints each
.I number
followed by its prime factors, one per line, each indented five spaces,
in non-decreasing order, repeated per multiplicity (so
.B 12
is followed by
.BR 2 ,
.BR 2 ,
then
.BR 3 ).
A blank line follows each number's factors.
.PP
With no arguments,
.I factor
reads numbers one per line from standard input, factoring each in
turn, until a line's value is zero or negative (which is treated as an
end marker, not itself factored or reported as an error) or standard
input ends.
.SH SOURCE
.B /p9/cmd/factor.b
(translated from
.BR sys/src/cmd/factor.c )
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR factortest (1),
.IR primes (1)
.SH BUGS
Every number here is Limbo's
.B real
(IEEE double), exactly matching the C original's use of
.B double
for the same reason
.IR primes (1)
does - see its BUGS for the range limit that follows from that choice.
.PP
The trial-division wheel used past the 2/3/5/7 pre-checks starts its
index at 1, not 0, in the original C - a real, easy-to-miss detail
carried over deliberately rather than "cleaned up" to match
.IR primes.b 's
own, differently-indexed wheel loop; the two files' wheels are
different sequences besides.
